<!-- rtdf-block-id: NSW_community_gaming/nsw_draw_lottery:b0002; role: preamble-definitions; provision-id: none; source-lines: none; relation: preamble -->
```catala
```


A draw lottery is a permitted gaming activity for the purposes of section 10 of the Act
if the following requirements are complied with—

(a) the gaming activity is conducted by or on behalf of a charitable organisation
or a non-profit organisation,

<!-- rtdf-block-id: NSW_community_gaming/nsw_draw_lottery:b0003; role: provision; provision-id: NSW_community_gaming/nsw_draw_lottery:p0001; source-lines: 2-6; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
```

(b) not less than 40% of the gross proceeds of the gaming activity are paid to the
benefiting organisation,

<!-- rtdf-block-id: NSW_community_gaming/nsw_draw_lottery:b0004; role: provision; provision-id: NSW_community_gaming/nsw_draw_lottery:p0002; source-lines: 7-8; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
```


(c) the total value of all of the prizes does not exceed $30,000.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: NSW_community_gaming/nsw_draw_lottery:b0005; role: provision; provision-id: NSW_community_gaming/nsw_draw_lottery:p0003; source-lines: 10-10; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
```

